title: room.enter
---
<<if not $hasLens>>
<<get lens>>
<<set $hasLens to true>>
<<endif>>
<<if $examinedFilings>>
<<cel filings 1>>
<<else>>
<<hide scratches>>
<<endif>>
<<if $openedClock>>
<<hide clock>>
<<cel caseDoor 7>>
<<else>>
<<hide caseDoor>>
<<endif>>
===

title: room.look
---
Thorne's workshop. A lantern burns, and of all the clocks here only the tall one in the corner is going. #line:102-001
===

title: clocks.look
---
<<closeup 240>>
Every dial reads seventeen minutes past three. #line:102-002
Hero: A fresh scratch beneath the minute hand. These clocks were stopped by hand. #line:102-003
<<set $examinedClocks to true>>
===

title: clocks.do
---
Hero: Let us preserve the evidence as we found it. #line:102-004
===

title: filings.look
---
<<if $examinedFilings>>
A trail of brass filings, from the bench to the tall-case clock. #line:102-005
<<else>>
Something glints in the sawdust, too fine to make out from here. #line:102-006
<<endif>>
===

title: filings.do
---
Hero: Best not disturb them. My lens will tell us more. #line:102-007
===

title: filings.lens
---
<<walk hero 196 158>>
<<face hero right>>
<<view hero 204>>
<<loop hero 1>>
<<animate hero once>>
Holmes kneels with his lens. Among the sawdust, brass filings catch the lantern light. #line:102-008
<<cel filings 1>>
<<show scratches>>
Hero: A trail from the bench to the tall-case clock. Something was recently fitted there. #line:102-009
<<normal hero>>
<<set $examinedFilings to true>>
===

title: scratches.look
---
Fresh scratches in the boards, where the case clock has been moved and moved back. #line:102-010
===

title: clocks.lens
---
Hero: The lens confirms it: each hand was turned and held. #line:102-011
===

title: clock.look
---
A tall-case clock of polished walnut, its pendulum swinging. The only clock in the shop still going. #line:102-012
Fresh scratches mark the boards beneath it. #line:102-013
===

title: clock.do
---
<<if $deduced>>
<<walk hero 214 160>>
<<face hero right>>
Hero: The clocks did not stop together. Someone arranged them so. #line:102-014
Hero: And this case is far too light for its size. #line:102-015
<<view hero 204>>
<<loop hero 0>>
<<animate hero once>>
<<stop clock>>
<<cel clock 0>>
<<hide clock>>
<<show caseDoor>>
<<sound 130>>
<<animate caseDoor once>>
<<normal hero>>
<<set $openedClock to true>>
<<wait 0.8>>
A stair behind the clock. The air from below is cold. #line:102-016
Hero: Come, Watson. Our clockmaker has left us a way in. #line:102-017
<<elseif $examinedClocks and $examinedFilings>>
Hero: Not yet. Watson, a moment. Let me put this in order aloud. #line:102-018
<<else>>
Hero: Before moving anything, I should examine the wall clocks and the filings on the floor. #line:102-019
<<endif>>
===

title: caseDoor.look
---
Behind the case, a narrow stair descends into darkness. #line:102-020
===

title: caseDoor.do
---
<<walk hero 262 166>>
<<room 103>>
===

title: stair.look
---
<<if $openedClock>>
Behind the case, a narrow stair descends into darkness. #line:102-021
<<else>>
The tall-case clock stands close against the wall. #line:102-022
<<endif>>
===

title: stair.do
---
<<if $openedClock>>
<<walk hero 262 166>>
<<room 103>>
<<else>>
Hero: Before moving anything, I should examine the wall clocks and the filings on the floor. #line:102-023
<<endif>>
===

title: lantern.look
---
The lantern is still warm. Thorne cannot have been gone long. #line:102-024
===

title: lantern.do
---
Hero: Leave it burning. We shall need the light. #line:102-025
===

title: window.look
---
The sash is latched. Rain runs down the glass, and the Clerkenwell roofs dissolve into the dark. #line:102-026
===

title: window.do
---
Hero: Secure from within. No one left by this window. #line:102-027
===

title: bench.look
---
A dismantled movement, a scribbled order and tools laid down in haste. #line:102-028
===

title: ledger.look
---
The last entry is unfinished. A deposit received for an unusual alteration to a clock case. #line:102-029
===

title: watson.look
---
I keep well clear of the evidence. Holmes has views on that. #line:102-030
===

title: watson.talk
---
-> What do you make of it? <<if not $examinedClocks or not $examinedFilings>>
    Watson: A locked room and a missing man. I make nothing of it yet. You? #line:102-031
    Hero: Nothing, until I have looked properly. #line:102-032
-> The clocks were stopped by hand. <<if $examinedClocks>>
    Hero: Every hand was turned to the same minute and held there. Look at the scratches. #line:102-033
    Watson: But why would a man stop his own clocks? #line:102-034
-> The filings lead to the case clock. <<if $examinedFilings>>
    Hero: Brass, freshly cut, from the bench to that tall-case clock. Something was fitted there, and recently. #line:102-035
    Watson: A repair, perhaps? #line:102-036
    Hero: In the middle of the night, with the door bolted? No. #line:102-037
-> The case clock is a door. <<if $examinedClocks and $examinedFilings and not $deduced>>
    Hero: Every clock here was stopped at the minute he went. All but that one. #line:102-038
    Hero: Its pendulum swings, yet its hands stand at seventeen past three, as still as the rest. #line:102-039
    Hero: It isn't keeping time, Watson. The filings lead to it. That case is a door. #line:102-040
    Watson: Then Thorne didn't vanish at all. He walked through it. #line:102-041
    <<set $deduced to true>>
===

